@title nonlinear193 — the folded gadget: one r57 gate c ^= a | !b over nonlinear encodings
@subtitle The replicated per-gate body: exactly 193 gates, deterministically (the '193' in the name). Every value 2-shared: v = E(v1) ⊕ E(v2), E(x0..x4) = x0⊕x1⊕maj(x2,x3,x4); ONE carrier (s2 majority) flipped by W = u⊕V, u = E(s1)⊕E(R) — the re-share is folded into the flip. Encoding setup and the 0-gate output relabeling are fixed infrastructure, not shown; borrows (R, ch) arrive on pool wires.
@equation c' = c ⊕ (a ∨ ¬b);   share1' = R,  share2' = (s2_0, s2_1, o0, o1, o2)  — the relabel costs 0 gates
@wire s1_0 scratch
@wire s1_1 scratch
@wire s1_2 scratch
@wire s1_3 scratch
@wire s1_4 scratch
@wire R0 R
@wire R1 R
@wire R2 R
@wire R3 R
@wire R4 R
@wire a1_0 scratch
@wire a1_1 scratch
@wire a1_2 scratch
@wire a1_3 scratch
@wire a1_4 scratch
@wire a2_0 scratch
@wire a2_1 scratch
@wire a2_2 scratch
